# L §7.1: key literals are allowed "in key positions: ... a comparison with a key (`allowance[u5]`, `k == pl`,
# `k <= 10` on an integer index)".  On ages = int 1..12, `k <= 10` is a key comparison, not a figure: a = 1 for
# k <= 10, else 0 (the bare 0 and 1 are inline figures, L §7.1). 
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index ages = int 1..12

def a[k in ages]: int at reader
  rule base = 0
  rule young beats base = 1 when k <= 10

ask q: a[10], a[11] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q: (1, 0)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
